  "notes": "A session guitarist turned producer, and the man behind the benchmark 90s female narrative ballad. Two progressions are documented from his own productions and they give the vocabulary directly: \"C–F/C–C–Gsus4 (I – IV/1 – I – Vsus4) on one hit, and an extended-piano-intro four-chord loop on another,\" with the entry naming \"the sus4-over-V and IV-over-tonic-pedal\" as his harmonic fingerprints — so I–IV–I–V leads the families and `susSubstitutionProb` is the highest of any producer here, because a sus is a quality the numeral parser cannot carry. The drum session is \"the most fully documented in this whole file,\" and the part of it that reaches a note generator is the grammar and the dynamic: \"cross-stick verse, 2&4 from the chorus, room-mic-driven fills into the final chorus,\" with the \"Sky Hook\" compressed room mic fourteen feet above the kit creating \"the explosive chorus character\" — authored as an accent tier that runs to the ceiling against a quiet main tier, not as a mic. The vocal method is the transferable arrangement parameter: \"six to seven complete takes per session, comped, with the singer doing 'homework' between sessions,\" i.e. a story-song build with a maximal final chorus. The palette adds \"orchestra bells sampled on a synthesizer as the high colour,\" which is the counter's bell echo. ⚠ The bass is \"live electric bass … root motion with walking pickups; no programmed low end,\" so no `bass808` block. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
